#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-tray: Claude Code usage and accounts in the panel.

Usage: claude-tray [--background | --test | --help | --version]

  (no option)    start the tray and open the dashboard, or open it if the tray already runs
  --background   start the tray without opening the dashboard (used at login)
  --test         print what the dashboard would show and exit (no window, no network)

The panel icon is a ring with the 5-hour usage of the account you used last: amber from 70%,
red from 90%, grey when the numbers are over 30 minutes old. Click it for the dashboard:
each account's 5-hour and weekly usage (the tick on a bar is where even spending would be),
today's activity across all accounts, the account with the most room left and the sessions
running now. Click an account to continue a session or open a project with it, log it in or
remove it. Sessions are shared, so a session started on one account continues on any other.

Usage numbers come from the status line (~/.claude-accounts/.usage). When an account's numbers
are over 5 minutes old the tray asks Anthropic's usage API with that account's own login.

Terminal: the first of kitty, gnome-terminal, konsole, xfce4-terminal, alacritty, wezterm,
foot, tilix and xterm that is installed; set CLAUDE_TRAY_TERMINAL to pick one.
Settings: ~/.config/claude-tray/settings.json      Log: ~/.cache/claude-tray/tray.log
"""
